1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,560
Today, I'm going to be focusing on making Minecraft as satisfying as possible using mods.

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:11,860
If a mod makes the game look satisfying, sound satisfying, or in general just add something that I'd consider satisfying, I'm going to include it.

3
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:16,500
And you know, Minecraft is already a pretty satisfying game, but we can always take that to the next level.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,980
Now, for this video, I'm mostly including mods that are going to be client-side, but I do have a few game-changing mods as well.

5
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:26,280
And I'll be sure to keep all the client-side mods first, just to avoid any confusion there.

6
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:33,760
And I have quite a few mods in this video, but if there's any others you'd like to see included, I may do a follow-up to this video in the future, so let me know.

7
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:35,400
So, anyway, let's go ahead and check it out.

8
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:42,600
So, to start things off, we're going to be installing a performance mod, because let's be honest, what's more satisfying than significantly enhancing your FPS?

9
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,080
This one, however, is going to come down to preference.

10
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:53,120
You can either use sodium along with iris, continuity, and indium for the best performance possible and overall most compatibility with the rest of the mod list.

11
00:00:53,120 --> 00:01:01,240
Or you can use Optifine, which generally doesn't perform quite as well as the other combination, but is pretty much an all-in-one mod and has quite a bit more features at this point.

12
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:07,480
Now, to start things off, we're going to take a look at Fresh Animations, which requires Optifine in order to, you know, actually work.

13
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:14,800
And this is easily one of my favorite things to have installed in Minecraft, because Fresh Animations adds amazing animations to most of the creatures in the game.

14
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:18,760
And with each update, it just continues to get better as it expands the mobs that are covered.

15
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:26,160
A list of satisfying mods would truly be incomplete without this mod, and its only downfall is that as of now, you can't use it with sodium.

16
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:31,560
As an alternative, however, if you'd like to go with sodium, you can always use the Better Animations collection mod.

17
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:39,000
And while in my opinion Fresh Animations is just a little bit better, this mod still provides plenty of really nice animations to many of the creatures in the game.

18
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:46,920
Next, I'll be installing the Stay True resource pack, and it's one of my favorite resource packs available, as it simply enhances the vanilla visuals.

19
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:53,880
Rather than completely changing the textures, it adds variance to them and makes them far less repetitive, and you'll also notice that blocks can blend together.

20
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:56,680
And really, at this point, you can go with whatever resource pack you like.

21
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,960
Whatever you find the most satisfying, go with that one.

22
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:03,240
But I decided to go with one that still just generally sticks to the vanilla appearance for this video.

23
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:07,760
Now, next up, we're going to hit another point where once again, you're going to need to make a choice.

24
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:10,440
Option one is Complimentary Shaders Reimagined.

25
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:20,160
The shader looks downright amazing and actually has some pretty great performance, and on the other hand, you can use the Distant Horizons mod, which allows you to run in Minecraft at pretty absurd render distances.

26
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,320
So really, it's up to you.

27
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:26,800
Would you rather be able to see really, really far away or have some absolutely fantastic lighting and visuals?

28
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,360
Either way, very satisfying.

29
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:35,680
And I would recommend picking one or the other, but I actually did find that if you use these two together while using OptiFine, they somewhat work together.

30
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:39,680
It's a little glitchy though, and the performance isn't great, which is to be expected.

31
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:42,640
But if you'd like to give this a try, you can definitely do so.

32
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:47,880
Alright, now for these next few mods, we're mainly going to be focusing on adding satisfying sounds to the game.

33
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:51,960
And first, we'll be installing Dynamic Surroundings Remastered Fabric Edition.

34
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:57,600
With this mod, you'll get beautiful biome sounds, some new visual effects, and amazing waterfall ambience.

35
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:04,880
And as I've mentioned before, waterfalls in Minecraft having actual waterfall sounds is immensely satisfying to me, so this is just a must-have.

36
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:09,400
And if the official version of Dynamic Surroundings ever gets updated, you can always use that one.

37
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,240
But for now, this is what we're sticking with.

38
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:18,000
We'll also be installing Presence Footsteps, which over the past 10 years now has provided incredibly satisfying footstep audio.

39
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,440
Not only do you get unique footstep sounds for most blocks, the mod also recognizes each foot on its own.

40
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:27,360
So now you can walk between two different blocks and the sound effect will alternate for each foot.

41
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,600
Very satisfying.

42
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:41,600
Next, I've included the Auditory mod, which adds a bunch of new sound effects, most notably for breaking and placing many of the blocks you can find in the game.

43
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:49,400
And this is something we've seen with many of the new blocks in Minecraft, for example Amethyst, and trust me, it's a wonderful thing hearing this feature brought to more blocks.

44
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:56,440
In addition to this, I've also installed Extra Sounds, which adds even more satisfying sounds to the game, mostly focused around the inventory.

45
00:03:56,440 --> 00:04:01,680
So when you scroll around, drop items, and move stuff around, you'll be fed all kinds of auditory goodness.

46
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:08,840
Now, moving on from sound-specific mods, everything else I've included really just covers a bit of everything.

47
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:15,560
For starters, we have Camera Overhaul, and this mod adds some pretty satisfying camera movement to the game, all depending on what you're doing.

48
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:19,800
And the default settings for this mod may be a bit nauseating for some people, but do not worry.

49
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:22,920
You can customize the intensity of each of these visual effects.

50
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:25,640
So if you'd like it to be subtle, you can absolutely do that.

51
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:29,520
And if you want to practically be doing barrel rolls when you move around, by all means, go for it.

52
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:36,080
Next, I've installed a pretty small mod called Disable Custom Worlds Advice that saves me from some pretty extraordinary anguish.

53
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:40,400
These incessant popups constantly letting me know that I, in fact, have mods installed.

54
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:42,800
Gone forever. It's really a beautiful thing.

55
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,560
And, in addition to that, I've installed Toast Manager.

56
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:51,960
And like Disable Custom Worlds Advice, this mod disables the constant achievement popups you get with each new world.

57
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:56,560
They're fun for the first few times, but can quickly get irritating when you just don't want them anymore.

58
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,520
After that, I've installed the Physics mod.

59
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:04,840
And this mod is just loaded to the brim with satisfying features, like mob rag dolls, block breaking physics, and much more.

60
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:08,520
And for the video, I'll be using the Pro version, which includes many more awesome features.

61
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:13,040
Now you'll see things like realistic smoke, better weather visuals, interactive snow, and much more.

62
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:16,960
And hey, if there's any features you don't enjoy with this mod, you can always just change or disable them.

63
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,000
Very satisfying.

64
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,400
I've also installed the InvMove mod, which allows you to move around while accessing inventories.

65
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,720
And this mod was surprisingly client-side.

66
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:30,640
I honestly thought this would be server-side, although I don't make any promises that you won't get banned if you use this on a server or something like that.

67
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:35,400
So if you do plan on using this mod online, I would definitely make sure you're allowed to use it on that server.

68
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:41,200
I've also included the Dynamic Crosshair mod, which changes slash hides your crosshair depending on what you're doing or holding.

69
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:49,160
And this can be especially nice when you have no need for a crosshair, as it frees up some of your HUD, making your game more beautiful and, by extension, satisfying.

70
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:55,240
Now, in order to make third-person more satisfying to use, I'll be installing it both better third-person and camera utils.

71
00:05:55,240 --> 00:06:03,080
Better third-person lets you walk around in every direction while playing in third-person, whereas camera utils allows you to customize exactly where the camera sits behind you.

72
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:07,240
And one of the last client-side mods we'll be installing for now is Legendary Tooltips.

73
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:10,960
And this mod simply lets you know when your valuables are in fact valuable.

74
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:14,800
Now they'll have a beautiful golden border that shows that that item is special.

75
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:22,240
And finally, for the last of our client-side mods, I've installed Effective, which adds several very satisfying water-based effects to the game.

76
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:30,280
Now you'll get some really nice visual effects when pretty much anything falls into water, and waterfalls appear much more powerful, I guess, as water splashes everywhere.

77
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:37,400
And this mod also has built-in waterfall sound effects, although I think Dynamic Surroundings does it just a bit better, so I've just gone ahead and muted these.

78
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:44,280
Alright, at this point, every single one of the mods we've installed is client-side, so if you want to use these mods on a server or with friends or something like that,

79
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:50,040
you won't be able to install any of the mods that are upcoming unless those mods are also installed on the server, so keep that in mind.

80
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:57,960
And like I said earlier, I'm not going to be installing that many server-side mods this time around, however, if I do another one of these videos, I'll be sure to include a lot more of both.

81
00:06:57,960 --> 00:07:00,160
So we're going to move on to a few server-side mods now.

82
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:03,760
And the first of these mods is both Better Combat and Combat Roll.

83
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:09,360
And these mods are both created by the same developer, and in combination, they make combat incredibly satisfying.

84
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:17,320
And you can also combine these mods with weapon mods like Miriam's Soulsborne Weaponry or Simply Swords to significantly expand the set of weapons available to you.

85
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:26,000
Next, I've selected diagonal fences just because being able to place fences diagonally is both mentally and visually pleasing, and overall just makes fences a whole lot more versatile.

86
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:37,240
And after that, I've installed Visual Workbench, which makes crafting pretty much infinitely more satisfying, as not only do items stay in the crafting table if you exit it, but they also stay on top and show exactly what you're crafting.

87
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:41,000
And truly, this mod just makes the entire crafting experience that much better.

88
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:48,640
And finally, the last mod I'll be showing today is Immersive Portals, and I still consider this to be easily one of those satisfying mods that exists.

89
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:56,360
I mean, when I first came across this mod's predecessor, Better Portals, I was completely mind-blown and really didn't even expect a mod like this to actually exist.

90
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:58,440
But it does, and it works pretty much perfectly.

91
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:07,440
I will mention, though, I was actually getting some crashes using this mod with this mod list, and I think the crashes were being caused due to incompatibility with the physics mod.

92
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:10,560
I'm not 100% sure on that, but I have my suspicions.

93
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:13,560
But hey, give it a try. You guys might have better luck with it than I did.

94
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,760
And anyway, that's gonna do it for this video.

95
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:24,000
And as I mentioned before, I would definitely love to do a part two, potentially beyond for this video, as there's many mods out there that I would consider very satisfying.

96
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,880
And I mean, yeah, I'd love to expand on it.

97
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:30,640
So be sure to comment some mods below, and I'll be sure to take a look at them and potentially include them in the future.

98
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:37,640
And anyway, let me know what you thought about this video, and if you guys enjoyed, be sure to leave a like, comment, and subscribe, and until next time, thanks for watching.

